# terraform/.trivyignore
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS:
# Trivy scans Terraform configs for security misconfigurations.
# Some findings are ACCEPTED for a demo/lab environment.
# Each entry must have a comment explaining why it is accepted.
# In a production environment, these should be fixed properly.
#
# To see all findings including ignored ones, run:
#   trivy config --ignorefile "" terraform/

# AVD-AWS-0104 / AWS-0104: Security group allows egress to 0.0.0.0/0 (all outbound).
# ACCEPTED: Servers need to reach apt repos, GitHub, GHCR, AWS APIs.
# In production: restrict to specific CIDRs/prefixes.
AVD-AWS-0104
AWS-0104
